{
  "id": "25536_hokansuru",
  "headword": "{保管|ほかん}する",
  "reading": "ほかんする",
  "romaji": "hokansuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to store; to keep; to hold in custody",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to store; to keep safely; to hold in custody; to preserve",
      "explanation": "To keep something in a safe or proper place for future use or safekeeping."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25536_hokansuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{書類|しょるい}を{保管|ほかん}する。",
      "english": "I store the documents.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25536_hokansuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{貴重品|きちょうひん}は{金庫|きんこ}に{保管|ほかん}してください。",
      "english": "Please keep valuables in the safe.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25536_hokansuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{薬|くすり}は{冷蔵庫|れいぞうこ}で{保管|ほかん}する{必要|ひつよう}があります。",
      "english": "This medicine needs to be stored in a refrigerator.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{保管|ほかん}する emphasizes safe, responsible keeping of items — often with the implication that they will be needed later or that they have value worth protecting. It is more formal than しまう and more focused on safekeeping than {保存|ほぞん}する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {書類|しょるい}を{保管|ほかん}する: store documents\n- {荷物|にもつ}を{保管|ほかん}する: store luggage\n- {冷暗所|れいあんしょ}で{保管|ほかん}する: store in a cool dark place\n- {保管|ほかん}{場所|ばしょ}: storage location\n- {保管|ほかん}{期間|きかん}: storage period\n- {保管|ほかん}{料|りょう}: storage fee\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {保存|ほぞん}する: to preserve; to save — focuses on maintaining condition over time, also used for digital file saving\n- しまう: to put away; to store — casual, everyday word for putting things in their place\n- {預|あず}ける: to leave in someone's care; to deposit — involves entrusting to another person or institution",
